  "id": "batticaloa_koothu",
  "name": "Batticaloa koothu (eastern Sri Lankan Tamil dance-drama)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Tamil dance-drama of the Batticaloa region on Sri Lanka's east coast, performed by village troupes in an open-air arena in two main styles, vadamodi (northern style) and thenmodi (southern style). An annavi, the troupe master, leads the singing to the maddalam drum and cymbals, and a chorus repeats the actors' sung lines. Research by S. Maunaguru and the Swami Vipulananda Institute of Aesthetic Studies has documented and revived it. A generic membrane-drum card stands in for the maddalam and the manjira card for the cymbals.",
  "recipe": "classic modern batticaloa koothu, ballad Poetry, indian bard branch. live take. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, manjira. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
